<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Aer Rianta airports operator 96 pretax up 13 pct.</title>
<headline>Aer Rianta airports operator 96 pretax up 13 pct.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>			     (million punts unless stated)</p>
<p> Pretax profit	     42.4		   vs 37.6</p>
<p> Capital expenditure     22.6		   vs 24.0</p>
<p> Net profit		  39.4		   vs 34.1</p>
<p> Turnover		    231.3		  vs 212.5</p>
<p> Total passengers (million)  11.96		  vs 10.57</p>
<p>    Of which: Dublin     9.10		   vs 8.02</p>
<p>		  Shannon    1.74		   vs 1.57</p>
<p>		  Cork	 1.12		   vs 0.97</p>
<p> Freight (tonnes)	  146,681		vs 124,000</p>
<p> Transfer to govt	  12.9		   vs 11.9</p>
<p>Average airport charge</p>
<p>   per passenger (punts) 3.29		   vs 4.39</p>
<p>NOTE - State-owned Irish airports operator Aer Rianta said 1996 was a record year for passenger numbers and it expected 1997 to be &quot;another excellent year&quot;.</p>
<p>--Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
